The test description says "should escape single quotes characters" but the plural "characters" should be singular "character" or the phrase should be reworded to "should escape single quote characters" for grammatical correctness.
```suggestion
  it('should escape single quote characters', () => {
    expect(safeJsString("./button.tsx'alert({ console.log('malicious code') })")).toMatchInlineSnapshot(`"./button.tsx\\'alert({ console.log(\\'malicious code\\') })"`);
  });

  it('should escape double quote characters', () => {
    expect(safeJsString('./button.tsx"alert({ console.log("malicious code") })')).toMatchInlineSnapshot(`"./button.tsx\\"alert({ console.log(\\"malicious code\\") })"`);
  });

